'''The Fallen''' is a [[boss]] that can appear on any main path [[Chapter]], with the prerequisite that Isaac has entered (not just encountered) a {{r|Devil Room}} through any methods, and with the following exceptions:

* It cannot appear on floors with predetermined bosses such as {{e|Mom}}, {{e|Mom's Heart}}, {{e|Isaac}}, etc.
* {{dlc|r}} It also cannot appear on any of the alternate Chapters added in [[Repentance]].
It is also encountered as the first phase of the {{e|Satan}} battle.

== Behavior ==
=== Phase 1 ===
The Fallen moves randomly around the room in cardinal directions and can perform the following attacks:
* Fires 3 projectiles in a spread followed by 4 projectiles in a spread in succession towards Isaac.
* Increases its speed and chases Isaac. After taking a certain amount of damage, it halts and fires a {{i|Brimstone}} laser in each cardinal direction.

=== Phase 2 ===
* At 50% health, The Fallen splits into two smaller versions of itself. The two clones have identical behaviour.
** It is possible to avoid the split if the Fallen takes a single hit doing more than 50% damage that causes [[poison]]ing or [[burn]]ing as the final one.
The Fallen deals a whole heart of contact damage in both phases.

== Notes ==
* Unlike other bosses, the item pool of the Fallen room is the [[Devil Room (Item Pool)|Devil Room item pool]].
** {{Dlc|na}}Leaving and re-entering the room will change the item pool to the normal Boss Room item pool.
* The Fallen can appear on the first floor during a Victory Lap if a Devil Room was entered during the previous lap. Even more rarely, it is possible to encounter him on a normal run if the first level was rerolled with {{i|Forget Me Now}} or a 5-pip {{r|Dice Room}} after visiting the Devil Room by teleporting with a {{p|Joker}} card, a {{e|Red Chest}}, or similar methods.

