== Trivia ==
* The Fallen appeared in the Halloween Update for the original ''The Binding of Isaac.''
* Under normal circumstances, the Fallen is one of six bosses (the other five being {{e|Conquest}}, {{e|Headless Horseman}}, {{e|Krampus}}, {{e|Baby Plum}} if spared, and {{e|Bumbino}} if he picks up enough coins) who drop or can drop active items upon defeat.
* The Fallen is both visually and behaviorally similar to Krampus.
* {{dlc|nr}}Despite the first phase of The Fallen having a death animation before splitting into clones, the clones themselves don't have a death animation. {{dlc|r}}The clones now have a death animation, like the main Fallen.
* {{dlc|a+}} Previously, only ''Crusade'' would play when The Fallen appeared as Satan's first phase. As of [[Booster Pack #5]], ''Cerebrum Dispersio'' also has a chance to play in this situation.
** This also applies to when the [[Angel]]s are fought normally (by bombing the Angel statues).
* The Boss might represent Satan or another fallen angel who fell from grace and became evil.
* The Fallen is tied with Krampus as having the highest [[Stage HP]] among all entities in the game.
* Double Trouble Fallen encounters in The Womb/Utero do not require the player to have entered a Devil Room before. Upon defeat, they will still drop a Devil Room item.
* The Fallen could appear in the alternative chapters in [https://antibirth.com/ Antibirth].

